<title>USA: Virginia Pwr sees 909 MW nuke on-line by Sun.</title>
<headline>Virginia Pwr sees 909 MW nuke on-line by Sun.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Virginia Power's 909 megawatt (MW) North Anna nuclear unit 2 is exiting a scheduled maintenance and refueling outage and should be back on-line this weekend, the company said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;We're warming up, and we should be back on-line by Sunday,&quot; said company spokesman Jim Norvelle, adding that the unit should return to full power about one to two days following the restart.</p>
<p>The unit, located in Mineral, Va., was shut on September 8.</p>
<p>Virginia Power is a unit of Dominion Resources Inc.</p>
<p>--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
